I reproduced this on `main` at `b702a5efbb74bebc056b798b414ddb923a82fbd5`. With an empty `examples/api-cache-query/node_modules/.vite`, `fullyParallel: true`, three Chromium workers and retries disabled, this probe failed on two pages and passed on one:

```ts
import { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'

for (const pageNumber of [1, 2, 3]) {
  test(`renders fetched posts on page ${pageNumber}`, async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/')
    await expect(
      page.getByRole('button', { name: 'The Model Is the Cache' }),
    ).toBeVisible({ timeout: 15_000 })
  })
}
```

The failed pages received `504 Outdated Optimize Dep`, missed `full-reload`, and kept an empty `#root` without sending `foldkit:request-model`. Every page should render the fetched posts. The same probe passed all three pages with a warm cache and with one worker.

A cold run with explicit includes for `@effect/platform-browser`, `effect/http`, `effect/persistence`, `@foldkit/devtools > clsx` and `foldkit > parse5` passed all three pages without an optimizer reload. The nested specifiers matter: bare `clsx` and `parse5` did not resolve from the example under pnpm.

I'll send a PR that declares these dependencies in the shared example client configuration and adds cold-cache coverage.
